{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Aaron's sons shall make it smoke</b> — a euphemism (כִּנּוּי) for the fire [offering] mentioned above: (Leviticus 3:3) \"and he shall present from the sacrifice of peace-offerings an offering made by fire (אִשֶּׁה) to YHWH,\" and it is equivalent to what is said below: (Leviticus 3:16) \"and he shall make them smoke,\" for there it alludes to all the portions [that are burned]. And its midrash (Sifra, chapter 14:10) [is]: \"and they shall make it smoke\" (here), \"and he shall make it smoke\" (Leviticus 3:11), \"and he shall make them smoke\" (Leviticus 3:16) — what does Scripture teach? \"And they shall make it smoke\" — the valid one and not the disqualified one. \"And they shall make [it] smoke\" — that he should not mix fats with fats. \"And he shall make them smoke\" — all of them at once."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:49:59.703439739Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}